  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {苦労|くろう}を{厭|いと}わない (not shy away from hardship)\n- {手間|てま}を{厭|いと}わない (not begrudge the effort)\n- {危険|きけん}を{厭|いと}わない (not shrink from danger)\n\nUSAGE:\nMost commonly encountered in the negative form {厭|いと}わない, meaning \"to not shy away from\" or \"to willingly accept.\" The affirmative form is less common in modern usage. The word has a literary, slightly elevated register — in casual speech, {嫌|きら}う or {嫌|いや}がる are more natural choices. The kanji {厭|いと} is relatively uncommon and the word is sometimes written in hiragana as いとう.",
